#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""journeymaxx: review a batch of user journeys from the terminal.

Claude writes journeys into a .journeymaxx file (JSON); you run `journeymaxx`
next to the Claude session and go through them: enter approves, c sends Claude
a message, v says it out loud (ElevenLabs speech-to-text), ctrl+g edits in vim,
r rejects.

  You:     journeymaxx                      review (TUI)
           journeymaxx talk                 review by voice: it reads each one out, you answer
  Claude:  journeymaxx add < journeys.md    queue journeys (markdown split by ---, or JSON)
           journeymaxx wait                 block until there is feedback, then print it
           journeymaxx feedback             print feedback not yet read
           journeymaxx revise ID -m "..."   new text on stdin, back to pending
           journeymaxx ask ID "..."         question or pushback he must answer, back to pending
           journeymaxx reply ID "..."       a note on the thread; stays out of his queue
           journeymaxx list | show ID | export
"""
